+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+MAIN-confirmed operation retains its standby and gas-release SET behavior. Initial AutoEngage=2 standby without MAIN history can grant one SET after observing released gas, a fresh press of at least 0.1s, and release with target/actual speed at least 30 km/h. Failure requires a new pedal cycle.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+After enabling, update and restart to apply the new Panda profile; verify CRUISE standby on the dash. Require 0.5s of initial valid observation and a trial within 0.1s of release. Gas held at restart must be released and pressed again.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+The initial indication alone cannot start cruise; only stock ON confirms MAIN. Explicit MAIN OFF, brake, CANCEL and invalid inputs block; retain six-frame/120ms pulses and existing retry intervals. ECU acceptance and vehicle behavior remain unverified.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
